From 8f54b5589376982baa15f7674371f143f32502b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:57:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix new-client product cards: dead click toggle,
 auto-selected defaults, off-brand color, oversized layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The card selection UI on /home/new had a real interaction bug: each
product card was a <label onClick=...> wrapping a checkbox with a
no-op onChange. Clicking a label natively forwards a click to its
wrapped checkbox, which bubbles back up through the label and fires
that onClick a second time — two toggles per click, canceling out, so
selecting/deselecting a product silently did nothing. Fix: toggle
logic now lives only in the checkbox's onChange; clicking anywhere on
the card still works via native label behavior, just without the
duplicate handler firing it twice.

Also:
- No products pre-selected by default — a new client's products are a
  real choice, not something to opt out of. createWorkspace already
  has a clean "select at least one" validation error for an empty
  selection, so this is a fully supported state, not a dead end.
- Swapped the selected-state/focus teal for amber, matching the accent
  used everywhere else in the app (toggle switches, selected states,
  focus rings).
- Tightened card padding/icon/text sizing and switched the grid from a
  fixed grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 (wraps awkwardly once there's an
  odd number of products) to auto-fit/minmax so cards stay equal-width
  in one row for however many products exist.
- Replaced the hardcoded reputation-manager/else-showtime icon lookup
  with product.image straight off WORKSPACE_PRODUCTS — the old
  fallback would have silently shown Cold Open with Showtime's logo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
